From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Martin=20Pu=C5=A1k=C3=A1=C4=8D?= <martin@icebear.sk>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:14:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: pwrctrl: apple-wifi: Add BCM4350 power sequence

The iPad Air 2 (J81) BCM4350 needs REG_ON, a 100 ms settle time and
then DEVICE_WAKE held asserted. iOS drives DEVICE_WAKE through
AppleEmbeddedPCIEPort::setDeviceWake() while the device is active, and
the Apple NVRAM sets device_wake_opt=1, which makes the firmware depend
on it to leave deep sleep. The validated J81 configuration ran with
DEVICE_WAKE asserted.

Add match data for pci14e4,43a3 that enables VDD (REG_ON, a
regulator-fixed on the PMIC GPIO), waits 100 ms and then asserts
DEVICE_WAKE, rolling VDD back if that fails. Power-off already
deasserts DEVICE_WAKE before VDD.

[Orchard: from mattonik/ipad-nixos b94d42f kernel/patches/0052-pcie-apple-t7000-j81-reg-on.patch, 0067-j81-wifi-deep-sleep-and-device-wake-toggles.patch, handed to Orchard by micro23 (ipadair2-omarchy 7ea2b2b); the PCIe host's direct D2207 register write becomes the endpoint's vdd-supply, and the device-wake test option becomes the default for BCM4350. DEVICE_WAKE is now asserted before link training, where 0067 asserted it after link-up]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-apple-wifi.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-apple-wifi.c b/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-apple-wifi.c
index 91df035e3..b78f290da 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-apple-wifi.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pwrctrl/pci-pwrctrl-apple-wifi.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 
 struct apple_wifi_pwrctrl_data {
 	bool pulse_device_wake;
+	bool assert_device_wake;
 	unsigned int step_delay_min_us;
 	unsigned int step_delay_max_us;
 	unsigned int stabilization_delay_ms;
@@ -39,6 +40,17 @@ static const struct apple_wifi_pwrctrl_data apple_j172_wifi_data = {
 	.stabilization_delay_ms = 100,
 };
 
+/*
+ * BCM4350 (iPad Air 2): REG_ON, 100 ms, then DEVICE_WAKE held asserted.
+ * iOS drives DEVICE_WAKE through AppleEmbeddedPCIEPort::setDeviceWake()
+ * while the device is active, and the Apple NVRAM (device_wake_opt=1)
+ * makes the firmware depend on it to leave deep sleep.
+ */
+static const struct apple_wifi_pwrctrl_data apple_bcm4350_wifi_data = {
+	.assert_device_wake = true,
+	.stabilization_delay_ms = 100,
+};
+
 static void apple_wifi_step_delay(const struct apple_wifi_pwrctrl *wifi)
 {
 	if (wifi->data->step_delay_min_us)
@@ -99,6 +111,17 @@ static int apple_wifi_power_on(struct pci_pwrctrl *pwrctrl)
 	if (wifi->data->stabilization_delay_ms)
 		msleep(wifi->data->stabilization_delay_ms);
 
+	if (wifi->data->assert_device_wake) {
+		ret = apple_wifi_set_device_wake(wifi, 1);
+		if (ret) {
+			rollback = apple_wifi_set_vdd(wifi, false);
+			if (rollback)
+				dev_err(pwrctrl->dev,
+					"failed to roll back VDD: %d\n", rollback);
+			return ret;
+		}
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -199,6 +222,10 @@ static const struct of_device_id apple_wifi_pwrctrl_of_match[] = {
 		.compatible = "apple,d111-bcm4355-wifi",
 		.data = &apple_iphone7_plus_wifi_data,
 	},
+	{
+		.compatible = "pci14e4,43a3",
+		.data = &apple_bcm4350_wifi_data,
+	},
 	{
 		.compatible = "pci14e4,43dc",
 		.data = &apple_j172_wifi_data,
